    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Myotonic dystrophy type 1 (DM1), a neuromuscular degenerative disorder, is\r\ncharacterized by a CTG repeat expansion (>100 CTGs) in the 3’ untranslated region of the\r\nDystrophia myotonica protein kinase (DMPK) gene. The leading hypothesis regarding DM1\r\npathology is that this expansion leads to the sequestration of splicing factors, which is\r\nresponsible for aberrant splicing events in insulin receptor gene (INSR), Cardiac troponin T\r\n(Tnnt2), and DMPK itself, resulting in severe muscular degeneration at the clinical level.\r\nHowever, studying genetic diseases such as DM1 has historically been complicated by the\r\ninherent genetic bias between cells from different sources, a complication that can now be\r\nremoved by using gene targeting technologies. The purpose of this research is to generate a\r\ngenetically unbiased model to study myotonic dystrophy’s pathology by targeting the expanded\r\nCTG repeat in the DMPK locus in patient-derived fibroblasts. A set of engineered nucleases,\r\ntranscription activator-like effector nucleases (TALENS) and RNA-guided nucleases\r\n(CRISPRs), were constructed to target the CTG expansion. To repair the CTG expansion, donor\r\nDNA with arms of homology to the DMPK gene and a normal number of CTG repeats were\r\nintroduced to serve as a template for correction via homologous recombination. By correcting\r\nthis expanded CTG repeat through gene targeting, aberrant alternative splicing events caused by\r\nthe sequestering of splicing factors at the expanded repeat can be further studied by analyzing the\r\nmRNA isoforms of genes known to be affected by the expanded repeat, such as INSR, Tnnt2,\r\nand DMPK. Creating this genetically unbiased model of DM can provide insight into what other\r\ngenes are involved in the pathology of the disease, providing an invaluable tool in developing\r\npotential therapeutics for this disease.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
